ent request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying, to avoid paging on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01AGHMRLG2C8EvpvKUeN5tsC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18. A SEV2 incident (INC-0001) is open and describes the rollback.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy. v2.3.0 had already run healthy in production, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed across regions. I retried the same rollback to v2.3.0, and it completed in all three regions.\n- **Incident:** The create-incident call timed out, so I checked the incident list before doing anything else. INC-0001 was already there with the full summary, so I did not open a duplicate.\n\nFollow-up for the on-call engineer: find the cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator partial failure, and decide whether v2.3.1 should be re-released.", "type": "text"}]}]}